\textbf{Solution:} Since point C is the midpoint of AB, and given points A(0,4) and B(6,0), it follows that point C(3,2), therefore CD=2, and OD=3; since CD is perpendicular to the x-axis, it follows that $\angle EOF=\angle CDF=90^\circ$. In $\triangle EOF$ and $\triangle CDF$, we have
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
\angle EOF=\angle CDF\\
\angle OFE=\angle CFD\\
EF=CF
\end{array}
\right.
\]
therefore, $\triangle EOF\cong \triangle CDF$ (by AAS), hence OE=CD=2, and OF=FD=$\frac{1}{2}$OD=$\frac{3}{2}$, therefore point F($\frac{3}{2}$,0), and point E(0,-2); Construct the symmetric point A$^{\prime}$ of point A with respect to line CD, and draw line A$^{\prime}$E intersecting CD at point F, draw line AP, thus point A$^{\prime}$(6,4). Suppose the equation of line A$^{\prime}$E is y=kx+b, then
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
6k+b=4\\
b=-2
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Solving this yields:
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
k=1\\
b=-2
\end{array}
\right.
\]
therefore, the equation of A$^{\prime}$E is y=x-2, when x=3, y=1, therefore point P(3,1) is $\boxed{(3,1)}$.

